{"uid":"c99c3a5e1305d0e3","name":"test_a_second_rejection_on_the_same_ruling_proceeds_instead_of_re_parking_again","fullName":"tests.test_ruling_re_park_bound#test_a_second_rejection_on_the_same_ruling_proceeds_instead_of_re_parking_again","historyId":"a34c176ea0bbbbf72dc9e5bce1b98469","time":{"start":1791925816476,"stop":1791925816591,"duration":115},"description":"Cure task cure-01-02-3 (PRD requirement A.5, #224): both rejections\n    below carry `raise_operator_gate: true` on their own reply -- the bound\n    is mechanical, not advisory, so a reviewer that keeps setting the field\n    on the SAME ruled signature still only buys ONE re-park, never a\n    second. Before this cure, the archive/replan tail's own combined check\n    ORed in the reviewer's field unconditionally alongside the mechanical\n    flag, so episode 3 below re-parked a second time on the identical\n    ruling with `rulingReparked` never gaining a fresh entry (the record\n    guard only fires when the ruling is NOT yet exhausted) while the\n    outcome stayed `paused` regardless\n    (`tests/_review_edges.py::test_A5_second_ruled_rejection_proceeds_after_reviewer_request`).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Cure task cure-01-02-3 (PRD requirement A.5, #224): both rejections<br />\nbelow carry <code>raise_operator_gate: true</code> on their own reply -- the bound<br />\nis mechanical, not advisory, so a reviewer that keeps setting the field<br />\non the SAME ruled signature still only buys ONE re-park, never a<br />\nsecond. Before this cure, the archive/replan tail's own combined check<br />\nORed in the reviewer's field unconditionally alongside the mechanical<br />\nflag, so episode 3 below re-parked a second time on the identical<br />\nruling with <code>rulingReparked</code> never gaining a fresh entry (the record<br />\nguard only fires when the ruling is NOT yet exhausted) while the<br />\noutcome stayed <code>paused</code> regardless<br />\n(<code>tests/_review_edges.py::test_A5_second_ruled